                            "MAJESTIC 12 / MJ-12\n===================\n\nClassification: Alleged secret government organisation.\n\nMJ-12 supposedly consisted of twelve senior military, intelligence and scientific officials established to investigate extraterrestrial contact and recovered spacecraft.\n\nThe story became widely known following the circulation of alleged classified documents during the 1980s.\n\nCLAIMED RESPONSIBILITIES:\n\n- UFO crash retrieval.\n- Alien biological examination.\n- Government secrecy.\n- Reverse engineering.\n- Public information management.\n\nDOCUMENTS:\n\n- Eisenhower briefing documents.\n- Alleged presidential memoranda.\n- Special access programme files.\n\nThe authenticity of MJ-12 documents is heavily disputed, and many researchers consider them fabrications.\n\nSTATUS: Unverified conspiracy theory.",
                        ),

                        "project-blue-book.txt": textFile(
                            "PROJECT BLUE BOOK\n==================\n\nOrganisation: United States Air Force.\nPeriod: 1952-1969.\n\nProject Blue Book investigated reports of unidentified flying objects.\n\nOBJECTIVES:\n\n- Determine whether UFOs represented a national security threat.\n- Analyse reported sightings.\n- Identify conventional explanations.\n- Evaluate unusual aerial observations.\n\nThe project investigated thousands of reports.\n\nA number remained unidentified at the conclusion of the programme.\n\nCONSPIRACY THEORIES:\n\nSome researchers argue that the programme was designed to ridicule witnesses or conceal genuine extraterrestrial encounters.\n\nOfficial investigations did not establish extraterrestrial visitation.",
                        ),

